# Copy to .env.local and edit. Vite only exposes variables that start with VITE_ to the browser.

# The site shows live Deadlock API data by default. Visitors can flip to sample data from the chip in the header, and the
# choice is remembered in their browser. Set this to fixture to make illustrative sample data the default for a build.
# VITE_DATA_SOURCE=fixture

# Where the browser sends API requests. The public API allows browser requests, so this can stay unset for local work.
# For a public site run your own proxy (npm run proxy) so one cache and one API key serve everyone:
# VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8787

# --- Livestreams (optional) ---
# Base address of the proxy's /streams route (the same proxy as above is fine). Leave unset and /streams shows sample streams.
# VITE_STREAMS_BASE=http://localhost:8787
# The proxy needs a Twitch application (https://dev.twitch.tv/console). These two stay on the server, never in the browser:
#   TWITCH_CLIENT_ID=...
#   TWITCH_CLIENT_SECRET=...
#   TWITCH_GAME_ID=...   (optional: skips looking the "Deadlock" category up by name)

# --- Live matches (optional) ---
# If you run a viewer that can open a match by id, put its address here with {id} where the match id goes.
# VITE_WATCH_URL_TEMPLATE=https://example.com/watch/{id}
